  "title": "Cortical dominance and cortical deference",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "6dd147cc-add9-485d-b615-3787b7e5d7b5",
      "text": "When input is rerouted to a nonstandard cortical target, cortical dominance means the qualitative expression of the area stays the same, as when stroking the face is felt in a phantom arm. Cortical deference means the area takes on the character of its new source of input.",
